{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. I understand you've been having trouble breathing for about three weeks now. Can you tell me more about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been getting worse. I’ve had this thick yellow mucus coming from my trach, and I just can’t catch my breath like before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned in the ER that this feels similar to when you had your last bronchoscopy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. Last time, after they cleared out the mucus, I felt so much better. I couldn’t get in for a scheduled bronch, so I came here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ve reviewed your history — you have relapsing polychondritis and SMAD4 syndrome, which cause your airway to narrow over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and I get monthly bronchoscopies to keep it open. But missing one really threw me off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve scheduled interventional pulmonology to do a bronchoscopy with balloon dilation tomorrow. That should help open up your airway and clear the mucus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be sedated, so you won’t feel much. Afterward, we may give you some pain medicine if needed. We did check your labs — your white blood cell count is high, but that’s common for you due to your condition and steroid use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. No fever this time, so it’s probably not an infection, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we think. Your chest X-ray shows no pneumonia or fluid. So we believe this is mostly mucus buildup from the stenosis. We’ll confirm more after the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2137-08-02 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds right. I just want to breathe normally again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, Mr. ___. You just got back from your bronchoscopy. Everything went well — they dilated your trachea and both main bronchi. They removed a lot of thick mucus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a little groggy, but my chest feels looser already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We also sent a sample of the washings from your airway to check for infection. We saw some gram-negative rods, which means we’ll start you on antibiotics just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Antibiotics? But I don’t have a fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "True, but because of your trach and frequent procedures, we don’t want to take chances. The culture grew Klebsiella oxytoca, which is treatable. You’ll take cefpodoxime for six days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take it. Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not usually, especially since it’s sensitive to the antibiotic. It’s likely from your own airway flora. We’re just being cautious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my breathing — should it keep improving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, over the next day or two. We’ll monitor your oxygen levels. You desaturated a bit when walking earlier, so we’ll keep an eye on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did feel short of breath just going to the bathroom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2137-08-03 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re ordering a CT scan tomorrow to make sure there’s nothing else going on, like a small area of infection or collapse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your CT scan came back. Good news — your airway looks stable, no new blockages or clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about the desatting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The scan showed some subtle inflammation in your lungs, but nothing acute. It’s likely related to chronic changes from your condition. Your oxygen improved with rest, so we think you’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m not getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you’re actually improving. Your white count is coming down — it was 14, now it’s 10.7. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about my regular meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re back on your usual — prednisone, methotrexate, folic acid, famotidine, calcium, vitamin D. We held losartan because your blood pressure was a bit low, but your PCP will restart it if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the inhaler?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adding Symbicort twice daily to help with airway inflammation and keep things open. It works with your other treatments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll use it. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you keep doing this well, probably tomorrow morning. We’ll make sure you can walk without desatting too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2137-08-04 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Interventional pulmonology will call you to schedule your next bronchoscopy. And please see your primary care doctor to review your meds, especially losartan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve made great progress. Your breathing is better, and your labs are improving. We’re clearing you to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep caring for your trach as usual, take all your meds — especially the cefpodoxime for the full six days. Finish the Symbicort as prescribed. And watch for fever, increased mucus, or trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel like I’m getting blocked up again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call interventional pulmonology. Don’t wait too long. And if you can’t reach them, come back to the ER. You know your body best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad we could help. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing — should I restart losartan on my own?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, please wait for your PCP to tell you. We held it because your BP was lower in the hospital, but they’ll decide when it’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Your care team will send instructions to your home. Someone from pulmonology should call within two days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "If I don’t hear, I’ll call them directly?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Don’t hesitate. We want to keep you stable and out of the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2137-08-05 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2137-08-02 19:59:00",
    "admission_end": "2137-08-05 16:26:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for progressive dyspnea and productive cough over three weeks, consistent with mucus accumulation due to recurrent tracheal stenosis from relapsing polychondritis and SMAD4 syndrome. He had missed a scheduled bronchoscopy and presented with increased yellow tracheal secretions. He underwent flexible bronchoscopy with balloon dilation of the trachea and both main bronchi, which relieved his symptoms. Bronchial washings grew Klebsiella oxytoca, prompting a seven-day course of cefpodoxime. A CT chest showed stable airway stenosis and no acute findings despite transient desaturation with ambulation. His white blood cell count improved from 14.0 to 10.7, and he was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to complete antibiotics, continue baseline medications, and follow up with interventional pulmonology and primary care.",
    "problems": [
      "Other specified diseases of upper respiratory tract",
      "Other specified congenital malformation syndromes, not elsewhere classified",
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Hypoxemia",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis"
    ]
  }
}
